          "english": "Marija: We have not seen each other for a while.",
          "source": { "kind": "site", "page": "getting_to_know.html", "file": "MQF - 2/Lesson 04/djalogu at the green grocer.pptx, slides 1-3, G10" }
        },
        {
          "slug": "qed-infittex-xoghol",
          "maltese": "Paolo: Bħalissa qed infittex xogħol.",
          "english": "Paolo: At the moment I am looking for work."
        },
        {
          "slug": "xtixtieq-tahdem",
          "maltese": "Marija: X'tixtieq taħdem?",
          "english": "Marija: What work would you like to do?"
        },
        {
          "slug": "nahdem-bhala-kok",
          "maltese": "Paolo: Nixtieq naħdem bħala kok. Minn dejjem kont inħobb insajjar.",
          "english": "Paolo: I would like to work as a cook. I have always liked cooking."
        },
        {
          "slug": "xoghol-ghal-qalbek",
          "maltese": "Marija: Nawguralek li ssib xogħol għal qalbek.",
          "english": "Marija: I hope you find work you enjoy."
        },
        {
          "slug": "se-jkolli-nhallik",
          "maltese": "Paolo: Issa se jkolli nħallik għax għandi intervista. Ħadt gost nitkellem miegħek.",
          "english": "Paolo: Now I will have to leave you because I have an interview. I enjoyed talking to you.",
          "note": "Se jkolli nħallik is a polite way to end the conversation: I will have to leave you."
        },
        {
          "slug": "hadt-gost-li-rajtek",
          "maltese": "Marija: Ħadt gost li rajtek.",
          "english": "Marija: It was nice seeing you.",
